# Build outputs under docs/data/ are split by whether they can be recomputed.
#
# COMMITTED (state — irreplaceable, accumulates across runs):
#   predictions_log.json   every pick ever published
#   accuracy.json          every graded result
#   model_baseline.json    the regression ratchet
#   video_intel.json       YouTube team news; CI cannot rebuild it, because
#                          YouTube blocks datacenter IPs for transcripts, so it
#                          is produced locally by youtube_intel.py and committed
#
# IGNORED (derivatives — CI rebuilds these from the state files every run):
#   model_weights.json     from model_fit.py
#   evaluation.json        from scripts/backtest_model.py --evaluate
#   calibration.json       from scripts/backtest_model.py --write
#   elo_ratings.json       from elo.py, replayed off accuracy.json
#
# Committing the derivatives meant every 30-minute CI run rewrote three files
# that any branch also regenerates, so every rebase collided on generated
# output. They still ship: the Pages artifact uploads the docs/ directory from
# disk, which gitignore does not affect.
docs/data/model_weights.json
docs/data/evaluation.json
docs/data/calibration.json
docs/data/elo_ratings.json
